<description>&lt;p&gt;Militant Islamist insurgents in Cabo Delgado beheaded six Christians, while a Catholic priest was killed after baptising 175 people, showing continued targeting of religious figures. Mozambican police killed three robbers at a micro-credit service, indicating security actions beyond the insurgency. The United States warned of a growing ISIS threat to African maritime trade, and abuses are reported to be undermining Mozambican counter-insurgency efforts. Oil prices rebounded after Hormuz shipping attacks, affecting regional economic expectations. The conflict caused 151 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTE5nUHJNZG5wNTNoTEJoeXYzWlhhNlIxcXFYclhQQVdKdkJ5d0ExWjBpR1NFRWpkSmQxeHd1dUNTYk1jaVpicXRFbi1za1p0WHhFWDJUNmlHbUlvM3NXTXc?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiV0FVX3lxTE1SdVpvLTl3Qi01N0RVTWxpRXZJdkg4ODlRa2NIRmZDWXlreTYzc3Fac3NMWTh2NFlwMS1POVlaTVVlUWVxbF9tUmI1OGxEQWdsektXdE1UQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;UN News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Business Insider Africa&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxOekF4RVlzcEdrclhSNE1OLTMwQWtMclFiS2ZjOTBQMTZxeTA2am84N043TXVMMFpBczJ6RFQyVUphVEF6al9fTUJxdXY0WkhLUXl6LW1LaUI0azZsdEN4dnVXNVd3RVFMWW9UMmx0MWU0RUx2cllyejN4WUZGcjRvYUx5S0loODBhZ0xzbkFaVVNIclZQMzU5bG9GMmh3Y1hOa1c0OUZwUUtoWnhmSE9Ka1ZRMWc?oc=5&quot;&gt;Truth Nigeria&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiowFBVV95cUxQVlkxb1dWU1dDS1RZX2dZQ3pCZkxmUWV1Ym5QTGpRV2FPQ2dSbG5WR1AyRmlaYWFvSnFkLWtyMHljcExacjdQTkd0dnEtMkttTEMwYmVDRUhMcTJrTHM3OXVJVklLVzRreW5iUGE2QjBUdVRXa2JEUVItbjRwWGlaR3k3eUNxWW1tWGMyaXk3VDZDbnIta2REY3BaYVlNM0dCU2hN?oc=5&quot;&gt;Club of Mozambique&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.googl